1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,640
Weddings are expensive affairs – there’s nothing new or surprising in that statement.
举办婚礼是件开销不菲的事——这话一点也不新鲜。

2
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:12,180
When we talk about the costs of a wedding, we often think about the financial toll on the person paying for it.
当我们谈论婚礼的花费时，往往会想到买单者要承受的经济压力。

3
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:22,010
The outlay on tiered cakes, the dress with a long train, appliques and veil, and canapes at the reception can all add up.
多层蛋糕、拖尾带贴花的婚纱和面纱、婚宴上的开胃小食，这些开销加起来数目不小。

4
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:23,820
But what about the guests?
但宾客们的开销呢？

5
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,440
The cost to your friends and family to attend.
那些前来赴宴的亲友们要付出的成本，却常常被忽略。

6
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:31,420
The first thing to think about when attending is the price of getting there.
出席婚礼，首先要考虑的就是往返路费。

7
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:38,460
Even just a few hundred miles from where you live can bring some expenses – be it transport or staying in a hotel.
哪怕只是离家几百英里的距离，也会产生交通费、住宿费之类的开销。

8
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:52,000
But some people like to tie the knot in exotic locations, thinking it will make their special day even more special – on a beach in front of palm trees rather than somewhere closer to home.
但有些人偏喜欢在充满异域风情的地方举办婚礼，他们觉得这样能让这个特殊的日子更难忘——比如在棕榈树环绕的海滩上，而非离家更近的地方。

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,130
Going to far-flung corners of the Earth to watch the event can really be a dealbreaker for some when deciding if they can make it.
对有些人来说，要远赴天涯海角参加婚礼，会成为他们决定是否出席的关键阻碍因素。

10
00:01:01,130 --> 00:01:03,750
Then there is the gift.
接下来就是礼金和礼物的问题。

11
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:06,340
What do you give a person on their wedding day?
婚礼当天，该给新人送点什么呢？

12
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:10,590
In some cultures, asking for money isn’t the done thing.
在一些文化里，直接索要礼金是不合时宜的做法。

13
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:16,340
Sometimes the bride and groom may issue a list of items they want to receive that you have to pick from.
有时新人会列出一份想要的礼物清单，让宾客从中挑选。

14
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,840
But what do you buy?
可到底该买什么呢？

15
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:20,850
And if it’s money, how much do you give them?
如果是送礼金，又该送多少？

16
00:01:20,850 --> 00:01:23,180
How much is too much?
多少算多哪？

17
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:31,860
These are questions all attendees face – give too little and you may cause offence, too much and you may be out of pocket.
这些都是每位宾客都会面临的难题——送太少怕失礼，送太多又会让自己手头拮据。

18
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:37,330
And of course, you don’t want to be outdone by a friend giving more than you.
而且，没人愿意在礼金数额上被朋友比下去。

19
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:44,810
Finally, the last thing you want to feel when going to a wedding is regret about the amount you’ve spent.
最后，参加一场婚礼，最不想感受到的就是为自己花出去的钱而后悔。

20
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:54,680
If you give a good gift and spend a lot on getting there, and the event isn’t great, or the food at the reception isn’t perfect, you might feel a little resentment.
如果你精心准备了贵重礼物，又花了不少钱奔波赴宴，结果婚礼办得不尽人意，或是婚宴的菜品难以下咽，心里难免会生出些许怨气。

21
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:59,380
Therefore, only give what you can afford to give.
因此，一切都要量力而行。

22
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:07,070
Weddings can be expensive for everyone concerned. But people often overlook the cost for guests.
婚礼对每个相关的人来说，都可能是一笔不小的开销，但人们常常忽略宾客的花费。

23
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:13,760
In the end, though, that special day is supposed to be a celebration of love above anything else.
不过说到底，这个特殊的日子，终究是一场以爱为核心的庆典。
